{"schema_version":2,"entity_type":"bundle","questions":[],"pools":[],"exercises":[{"client_key":"recovery_modal_verbs_recover","title":"Modal Verbs — Recupera","description":"Ricostruisci significato e forma di can, must, have to e should.","instructions":"Decidi prima se stai parlando di capacità, obbligo, divieto, scelta o consiglio.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","estimated_minutes":12,"settings":{"display_mode":"one_at_a_time","feedback_timing":"question_end","show_score":false,"show_correct_answers":true,"show_explanations":true,"show_diagnostic_summary":true,"allow_retry":true},"sections":[{"client_key":"recovery_modal_verbs_recover_section","title":"Recupera","instructions":"Decidi prima se stai parlando di capacità, obbligo, divieto, scelta o consiglio.","selection_mode":"fixed","feedback_timing":"question_end","questions":[{"client_key":"recovery_modals_recover_teaching","type":"content_block","title":"Modal verbs: scegli dal significato","prompt":"Prima di esercitarti","instructions":"Leggi le regole e osserva gli esempi.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","subtopic":"core","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Choose and form basic modal structures from communicative meaning.","difficulty":"support","content":{"educational_schema_version":1,"template_id":"educational-content-block-v1","variant":"grammar","body":"I modali non sono intercambiabili: la forma corretta dipende da ciò che vuoi comunicare — capacità, regola, divieto, opzione o consiglio.","intro":"Per uno studente italiano il contrasto decisivo è spesso mustn't / don't have to. Prima chiediti se una cosa è vietata o semplicemente facoltativa.","sections":[{"key":"can","type":"rule","title":"Can: capacità, permesso e possibilità semplice","body":"Can + verbo base esprime soprattutto ciò che una persona sa/può fare, un permesso semplice o una possibilità generale. Nelle domande can va prima del soggetto.","examples":[{"text":"I can swim.","highlight":["can swim"]},{"text":"Can I use your charger?","highlight":["Can I use"]},{"text":"It can get very cold here in winter.","highlight":["can get"]}]},{"key":"modal_form","type":"pattern","title":"Can, must, should + verbo base","body":"Dopo can, must e should usa direttamente la forma base: niente to e niente -s.","pattern":"subject + can/must/should + base verb","examples":[{"text":"She can drive.","highlight":["can drive"]},{"text":"You must stop.","highlight":["must stop"]},{"text":"He should rest.","highlight":["should rest"]}]},{"key":"obligation","type":"comparison","title":"Must e have to: obbligo","body":"Entrambi esprimono obbligo. A questo livello usa must per un obbligo forte o dato direttamente dal parlante; have to per una regola o necessità esterna. Nella terza persona: has to.","correct":{"text":"You must be quiet now. · Marta has to wear a uniform at work.","highlight":["must be","has to wear"]},"incorrect":{"text":"Marta have to wear a uniform.","highlight":["have to"]}},{"key":"prohibition","type":"comparison","title":"Mustn't ≠ don't have to","body":"Mustn't significa 'è vietato'. Don't have to significa 'non è necessario': puoi farlo se vuoi.","correct":{"text":"You mustn't park here. · You don't have to bring food; lunch is provided.","highlight":["mustn't","don't have to"]},"incorrect":{"text":"You mustn't bring food. (= non è necessario)","highlight":["mustn't"]}},{"key":"advice","type":"rule","title":"Should: consiglio","body":"Should/shouldn't dà un consiglio: è una buona o cattiva idea, non una regola obbligatoria.","examples":[{"text":"You should revise a little every day.","highlight":["should revise"]},{"text":"You shouldn't stay up all night before the exam.","highlight":["shouldn't stay"]}]},{"key":"have_to_form","type":"pattern","title":"Have to segue il Present Simple","body":"Have to non si comporta esattamente come can/must/should: usa has to con he/she/it e do/does nelle domande e negative.","pattern":"I/you/we/they have to · he/she/it has to · don't/doesn't have to · Do/Does ... have to?","examples":[{"text":"She has to leave early.","highlight":["has to"]},{"text":"Does he have to pay?","highlight":["Does","have to"]},{"text":"He doesn't have to pay.","highlight":["doesn't have to"]}]},{"key":"recap","type":"recap","title":"Prima di continuare","points":["Can: capacità, permesso, possibilità semplice.","Must: obbligo forte; mustn't: divieto.","Have to: obbligo/necessità esterna; don't have to: non necessario.","Should: consiglio.","Can/must/should + verbo base, senza to.","Have to usa has/do/does come un verbo al Present Simple."]}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":0,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":[],"fallback_error_code":null},"tags":["recovery","modal-verbs","recover","structured-teaching"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_modals_recover_1","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Una capacità","prompt":"Nina speaks English and Spanish, but she does not know Japanese. Which sentence is true?","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","subtopic":"ability","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Use can + base verb for ability","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"Nina can speak Spanish.","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"Nina cans speak Spanish.","is_correct":false,"error_code":"A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"},{"key":"c","text":"Nina can to speak Spanish.","is_correct":false,"error_code":"A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Can non prende -s e non prende to: can speak."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS","CORE_CAN"],"fallback_error_code":"A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"},"tags":["recovery","modal-verbs"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_modals_recover_2","type":"dialogue_choice","title":"Chiedere permesso","prompt":"Which question is appropriate?","instructions":"Leggi il dialogo e scegli la risposta più naturale.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","subtopic":"permission","primary_skill":"interaction","learning_objective":"Use can in a basic permission question","difficulty":"support","content":{"scenario":"A student wants to leave class for two minutes.","response_prompt":"Which question is appropriate?","turns":[{"key":"turn_1","speaker":"Student","text":"Excuse me, I need some water."},{"key":"turn_2","speaker":"Teacher","text":"Of course. What do you need?"}],"options":[{"key":"a","text":"Can I go and get some water?","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"Do I can go and get some water?","is_correct":false,"error_code":"A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"},{"key":"c","text":"Can I to go and get some water?","is_correct":false,"error_code":"A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Can va prima del soggetto: Can I go...?"},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"],"fallback_error_code":"A1_CAN_ABILITY_REQUESTS"},"tags":["recovery","modal-verbs"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_modals_recover_3","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Una regola","prompt":"At this laboratory, safety glasses are compulsory for everyone. You ___.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","subtopic":"external_obligation","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Choose have to for a clear external requirement","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"have to wear safety glasses","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"should wear safety glasses if you want","is_correct":false,"error_code":"A2_MODALS_OBLIGATION_ADVICE"},{"key":"c","text":"don't have to wear safety glasses","is_correct":false,"error_code":"MODALS_OBLIGATION_PROHIBITION"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"È una regola obbligatoria esterna: have to."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["MODALS_OBLIGATION_PROHIBITION","A2_MODALS_OBLIGATION_ADVICE"],"fallback_error_code":"MODALS_OBLIGATION_PROHIBITION"},"tags":["recovery","modal-verbs"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_modals_recover_4","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Vietato o facoltativo?","prompt":"The sign says “NO PHONES DURING THE EXAM”. Students ___.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","subtopic":"prohibition","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Distinguish prohibition from absence of obligation","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"mustn't use their phones","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"don't have to use their phones","is_correct":false,"error_code":"MODALS_OBLIGATION_PROHIBITION"},{"key":"c","text":"should use their phones","is_correct":false,"error_code":"A2_MODALS_OBLIGATION_ADVICE"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"NO PHONES = divieto: mustn't."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["MODALS_OBLIGATION_PROHIBITION"],"fallback_error_code":"MODALS_OBLIGATION_PROHIBITION"},"tags":["recovery","modal-verbs"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_modals_recover_5","type":"select_gap","title":"Terza persona","prompt":"Completa.","instructions":"Completa scegliendo la forma corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"modal-verbs","subtopic":"have_to_form","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Use has to and does not have to with third-person singular meaning","difficulty":"support","content":{"text_template":"Sara works at a hotel. She [[blank_1]] start at 7 a.m. on Mondays, but she [[blank_2]] wear a jacket; the uniform is optional.","blanks":[{"key":"blank_1","accepted_answers":["has to"],"opti